  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened labour administration system in Suriname</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme supports the modernization and capacity building of Suriname&apos;s labour inspectorate, focusing on developing and implementing strategic compliance plans. It also addresses child labour commitments under the Regional Initiative and compliance with Conventions C138 and C182. The programme aligns with Suriname&apos;s Decent Work Country Program (DWCP) 2023-2026, which prioritizes jobs, productivity, sustainable growth, livelihoods, human capital, and labour market governance.

The ILO will provide technical expertise, training, and capacity building to strengthen the labour inspection system and support child labour prevention. This includes developing special procedures, enhancing monitoring and reporting, and facilitating cooperation with other government agencies and social partners. The initiative aims to improve labour market governance, protect children, and ensure decent work and fundamental rights for all Surinamese.</narrative>
  </description>
